  "body": "Part of #2525 (slice 5 of 6). The maintainer set the priority on 2026-11-18: \"GPU shader issues get priority\".\n\nDepends on #2615 (GPU evaluator) and relates to #31 (the app on wasm).\n\n## What to add\n\n- The browser cannot block on the GPU. The native readback in `crates/ui/src/trace.rs` is native only (lines 28-30), and `headless_gpu::device()` is native only. Add an async readback path for the nest evaluator on `wasm32`, as `headless_gpu::device_async` does for the device.\n- On browser WebGPU: use the GPU evaluator of #2615.\n- On WebGL2: WebGL2 has no compute shaders (`DownlevelFlags::COMPUTE_SHADERS` is missing). Use the CPU evaluator of #2613. Log the reason one time.\n- The nest result is the same in the browser, on native and in the CLI.\n- The UI must not freeze during a long nest in the browser: run the search in steps across frames, or in a web worker if #31 has one. Show progress and permit cancel.\n\n## Notes\n\n- No new dependency: wasm-bindgen and the web runner are already in the lock (`Cargo.toml` lines 73-80). If the work needs a new crate (for example a worker helper), stop: that needs the owner's decision at review.\n- No new MCP tool.\n- Changes the path that computes nest positions: `effort:high`.\n\n## Done means\n\n- The `wasm32` target builds with the nest evaluator.\n- A native test runs the async evaluator path with a blocking executor and gives the same layout as the CPU evaluator.\n- A test forces the \"no compute\" case and shows the CPU fallback.\n",
